 0.368.\nCORRELATION: strongly positive, rho = +0.45 — a high-bp-vol decade and a failed bond hedge are the same fiscal-dominance / eroding-convenience-yield regime, which is the same regime as my CQ4 branch N. JOINT = 0.50 x 0.368 + 0.45 x sqrt(0.50x0.50x0.368x0.632) = 0.184 + 0.109 = 0.293, shaded to 0.28 because the branch-R world (38%) drags BOTH legs together by more than a single linear rho captures: managed curves suppress realized rate vol and a backstopped sovereign restores the hedge. Frechet check: 0.28 <= min(0.50, 0.368). CQ5 = 28. DRAFTING POINTS adopted from the Auditor and confirmed by two panelists: \"(or rise by >=25bp)\" is strictly REDUNDANT — any rise of >=25bp already fails to fall by >=50bp — so the parenthesis does not loosen the bar and a reader treating it as a second independent path over-rates the conjunct; and the \"equity drawdown window\" endpoints are undefined, with peak-DATE-to-trough-DATE the only reading that resolves, which favours long slow bears over sharp crashes.","referenceClassIds":[],"schemaVersion":"forecast-workbench.forecast/v1","sealedAt":"2026-11-04T17:31:53.957Z","seriesId":"published-panel","strongestContraryCase":"Not elicited per question. Panelist falsification signposts: {\"signpost\":\"G7 GDP-weighted 10y sovereign real yield (10y nominal benchmark minus 10y inflation swap / breakeven, computed on the same seven benchmarks) averages between 1.70% and 2.60% in EVERY one of 2030, 2031 and 2032, with no G7 sovereign having adopted explicit yield-curve control, a statutory captive-holding mandate for banks or insurers, or a central-bank 'market functioning' purchase programme above 3% of GDP.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2032\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"This is the signpost most specific to ME, because my distinguishing claim is not the level but the BIMODALITY: a three-year run inside a 90bp band with the policy branch unfired says the distribution is unimodal and my 54% branch-switch variance attribution is wrong. CQ4 collapses to roughly P10 1.60 / P50 2.20 / P90 2.90 (narrower, not shifted), the variance attribution reverts to premium-dominant (~50%) as the Wave-1 panel had it, CQ5 falls from 28 to ~22 because the bimodal-switch channel that fattens the rate-vol distribution disappears, and ~4pp moves from CQ6-C into B.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"The New York Fed HLW r* estimate for the United States (or the Richmond Fed Lubik-Matthes companion) is published at or below 1.0% for both the 2028 and 2029 vintages with no upward revision to the 2024-27 history, WHILE the US 10y TIPS real yield (FRED DFII10) averages below 1.70% over any rolling twelve months in the absence of any announced YCC, duration-shortening or captive-buyer mandate.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2031\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Kills my partial concession to the red-team that the filter is revising into a regime break, and vindicates the Wave-1 low-and-flat r* I moved away from. r* falls from 1.05% to ~0.80%, CQ4 P50 drops ~30bp to ~1.85 with P90 to ~2.80, CQ6-D rises from 13 to ~18 and CQ6-A falls ~2pp (cheap duration signals abundant saving, which is the demand-shortfall regime), and my CQ2 conjunct A rises ~4pp as the duration-price-versus-price-level substitution reverses.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"Japan's 10y JGB nominal yield stays below 2.25% AND Germany's 10y Bund below 3.00% on a twelve-month average, with the Bank of Japan holding a policy rate at or below 1.0%, in both 2031 and 2032.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2032\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Removes the Japan/euro convergence-upward component worth ~+25-35bp of my CQ4 recomposition — the component the Mechanism Modeler described in words and then neutralized, and that I restored. CQ4 P50 falls ~30bp to ~1.85 and the whole distribution shifts down without changing shape; CQ5 falls ~3pp through the MOVE level channel; CQ3 and CQ6 are essentially unchanged, because this is a price signpost, not a quantity one. It would also mean my 50/50 PPP-versus-market-FX weighting split mattered less than the component levels.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"Operational data-centre electricity across OECD-38 + China (strict operational definition) reaches 1,000 TWh/yr or more in 2036 WHILE cumulative announced-buildout impairments and cancellations exceed 20% of announced hyperscaler capex — i.e. the quantity arrives AND the write-downs arrive together.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2036\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"CONFIRMS the red-team's reversal that I adopted against the Wave-1 unanimous direction — that AI-Q3 is a quantity question gated by interconnection queues, transformers and licensed electricians rather than a financing question gated by the term premium, so a higher cost of capital changes who owns and who writes down the asset, not the megawatts. The converse observation (Q3 below 900 TWh with impairments above 20%) would falsify it and restore the Wave-1 coupling direction, moving my coupling note's Q3 call from flat-to-up back to down and raising the weight I place on the loanable-funds channel in r* from +5bp toward +15bp.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"An MSCI World peak-to-trough drawdown of >=25% occurs and G7 GDP-weighted 10y nominal sovereign yields fall by >=100bp from the equity peak date to the trough date — the bond hedge works emphatically, not marginally — while the trailing MOVE average since Jan 2027 is still below 100.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2033\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Consumes CQ5's most likely qualifying episode with a non-qualifying case and confirms the Wave-1 disinflationary-bust premise against the red-team's credit-event argument that I partly accepted. CQ5 falls from 28 to ~13 (short remaining window, both conjuncts weakened simultaneously). It also implies abundant precautionary saving, so CQ4 P50 falls ~30bp and my repression branch probability falls from 0.38 toward 0.28 (a sovereign that still rallies in stress needs no policy backstop); CQ6-D rises from 13 to ~18 at B's and C's expense.\"}","updateBasis":{"kind":"launch","note":"run1 wave 3 reconciler seat, effort 'rstar'."}}